ring but never passes it to compile-graph, so escalations run the approval node immediately with a nil approval and the human-in-the-loop gate is inert.", :status "2 fixed this wave (3312, 4100); cloud-itonami-isic-889 OUTSTANDING"}, :actor-never-compiled {:scope "isic-4100", :detail "g/compile does not exist in langgraph.graph (it is compile-graph) so the symbol resolved to nothing, and :end was used as a terminal node without being registered. Tests passed because no test loads that ns and the :run alias pointed at a building.sim that does not exist.", :status :fixed-this-wave}, :governor-rule-always-fires {:scope "isic-3312", :detail "unverified-client-violations read (or subject (:client-id subject)); subject is a map and truthy, so the whole map became the client id and every dispatch/order-parts proposal HARD-held on :client-unverified regardless of data, making a clean lifecycle unreachable.", :status :fixed-this-wave-with-regression-tests}, :ledger-records-rejections-not-grants {:scope "architectural, incl. the isic-9522 reference", :detail ":commit appends :committed and :hold appends :governor-hold/:approval-rejected, but :approval-granted is emitted only into the in-memory :audit channel and never appended. Approver identity survives on the commit record :payload :approved-by. Consequence in the reference: status-cell tests for :approval-granted against the ledger, a branch that is unreachable by construction.", :status :unfixed, :caveat "an earlier proxy grep of store.cljc produced a 462/464 figure; that proxy is invalid because the facts are emitted in operation.cljc. The figure is withdrawn and NOT recorded here."}, :approver-identity-dropped {:scope "isic-1394", :detail "operation/request-approval sets :approved-by on :payload while store/commit-record! reads :value, so the approver is not persisted at all (distinct from the architectural gap above, where it is persisted elsewhere).", :status :unfixed}}, :skipped-already-main 0, :not-done ["phase-1 containment inversion in 31 repos — a governance defect, belongs in its own task not an item-2 wave" "cloud-itonami-isic-889 interrupt-before still not wired" "skill industry-stack-wave step 2 already-real test is too weak: it accepts a file that calls the real actor with fabricated inputs; needs an input-provenance check (subject ids present in the store seed, no rendered field absent from the domain model)" "docs/index.html does not link the console in most repos (only 4311 added it)" "no nightly regeneration gate (flagship item 4) — would be a murakumo fleet gate, not GitHub Actions" "isic-1394 approver identity dropped"], :pool-before 250, :note "24/24 landed, 0 failed. Concurrency capped at 20 by the harness (CLAUDE_CODE_MAX_CONCURRENT_SUBAGENTS), so 4 repos were queued and launched as slots freed rather than run 24-wide. Every merge verified on main by fetching render_html.clj and operator-console.html sizes, not by trusting agent self-reports.", :type :industry-stack/wave, :merged 24, :parallel 20, :pins-verified 24, :requested-parallel 24, :success 24, :done-before 79, :failure-rate 0}
#:event{:wave 5, :verification "every merge verified on main by fetching render_html.clj and operator-console.html sizes; all 20 console sizes match the agent self-reported figures exactly. All 20 west pins verified fast-forward and reachable from the default branch. Pin advances were re-applied on top of the current origin/main after discovering the worktree base was 8 commits behind and would have reverted another session's pin.", :wave-mechanics {:tmp-collision "4 of 20 agents got false determinism mismatches because sibling agents wrote the same shared /tmp scratch path (isic-2022 clobbered isic-5012; isic-4520 clobbered isic-5120). All re-verified under mktemp -d and got byte-identical output, so no artifact is affected. The skill prompt says to render to a scratch path without requiring it be repo-local or mktemp -d.", :resource-guard-violation "isic-2651 briefly ran three concurrent clj-kondo JVMs, violating the one-heavy-build-at-a-time governor rule in CLAUDE.md", :good-patterns ["isic-2513's -main throws rather than write a console with zero :governor-hold facts, turning the HARD-hold requirement into an enforced build-time invariant instead of a convention" "isic-2431 screenshotted the result and fixed two real rendering defects; it was the only agent that did, and it was the only one that could have found them" "isic-4911 labelled :phase-disabled as a phase gate and :approver-rejected as the approver layer rather than inflating the HARD-hold count"]}, :merged-new ["cloud-itonami-isic-1040" "cloud-itonami-isic-1104" "cloud-itonami-isic-2022" "cloud-itonami-isic-2431" "cloud-itonami-isic-2513" "cloud-itonami-isic-2651" "cloud-itonami-isic-2731" "cloud-itonami-isic-3020" "cloud-itonami-isic-3230" "cloud-itonami-isic-3313" "cloud-itonami-isic-3520" "cloud-itonami-isic-4220" "cloud-itonami-isic-4312" "cloud-itonami-isic-4520-carwash" "cloud-itonami-isic-4620" "cloud-itonami-isic-4723" "cloud-itonami-isic-4911" "cloud-itonami-isic-5012" "cloud-itonami-isic-5120" "cloud-itonami-isic-5221"], :at "2026-08-12", :fail 0, :superproject-adr "2608090800", :already-real ["cloud-itonami-isic-0124" "cloud-itonami-isic-1399" "cloud-itonami-isic-2392" "cloud-itonami-isic-2813"], :findings {:mock-console-already-committed {:scope "isic-4620", :detail "docs/samples/operator-console.html existed since the initial commit as a hand-written mock, not actor-driven. Presence of a console file is therefore not evidence of item-2 completion anywhere in this fleet; any audit keyed on file presence scores such a repo green.", :status :fixed-this-wave}, :fabricated-inputs-in-committed-tests {:scope "isic-3020", :detail "the repo's own sim.cljc and operation_graph_test.clj drive defect-002/003/004, which are absent from the store seed. The agent declined to copy the pattern and derived its scenario from the seed instead.", :status :unfixed}, :approved-by-dropped-is-architectural {:detail "request-approval sets :approved-by on the record :payload while commit-record! persists :value, so the approver is never stored. Wave 4 recorded this as an isic-1394-specific bug; isic-2731 and isic-2513 hit it independently this wave in unrelated repos. It is a shared-scaffold defect, not a per-repo one.", :status :unfixed, :handling "2731 removed the dead column; 2513 rendered the approver from the run timeline, where it genuinely exists"}, :governor-keyword-message-bug {:scope "isic-3020", :detail "release-forbidden-violations and process-control-block-violations build their message with (some #(contains? kws %) words), which returns true rather than the matched word, so every hold detail reads 禁止キーワード 'true'. No test caught it because no test rendered the message.", :status :unfixed-out-of-scope, :found-by "rendering real output"}, :dads-markup-defects-found-only-by-browser {:scope "isic-2431, likely others", :detail "a dads-notification-banner used without its icon slot renders its heading one character per line, and white-space:nowrap clips wide tables. Found by headless-Chrome screenshot and fixed in 2431 only. The other 19 consoles were verified structurally (tag balance, text extraction) and never rendered, so DADS-styled ones may carry the same defects.", :status :fixed-in-2431-only, :follow-up "screenshot the 8 DADS-styled consoles from this wave"}, :sim-broken-on-main {:scope "isic-3520", :detail "gas.sim calls operation/run-operation, which does not exist in gas.operation (only build), so clojure -M:dev:run is broken on main. Pre-existing, untouched.", :status :unfixed}, :unreachable-human-gate {:scope "isic-3020 and others", :detail "interrupt-before is unreachable with seeded data where all advisor confidences exceed the floor and the only seeded defect is safety-critical (a HARD violation pre-empts the soft escalate branch). Agents stated this rather than fabricating input to reach it.", :status :informational}, :ledger-entry-was-unreadable {:detail "the Wave 0 entry was pretty-printed across 14 physical lines. This ledger is line-delimited EDN read line-by-line, and the tick's done-from-project-ledger swallows parse errors with (catch :default _ acc), so that entry contributed nothing to the done-set fallback and failed silently. Repaired by re-serialising each entry to one line; verified no data lost (58 repo names and 10 shas before and after).", :status :fixed-this-wave, :lesson "a reader that swallows parse errors turns malformed data into missing data with no signal"}, :skeleton-repo-needed-seed {:scope "isic-1104", :detail "no langgraph, advisor.cljc a stub, sim.cljc printing not-yet-implemented. store/seed-db, all-batches and full-evidence-checklist were added to drive the actor at all, with seed-db taking now-epoch-ms from the caller so store.cljc stays free of host-clock calls. Its run-operation returns {:ok? true :facts []} on a clean verdict, so that ledger can only ever hold :governor-hold.", :status :built-with-wider-scope}, :ledger-fact-shape-varies {:detail "isic-3520 governor-hold facts carry :violations, not :basis. The reference's (-> f :basis first) does not generalize across the fleet.", :status :informational}}, :skipped-already-main 4, :not-done ["isic-3020 governor keyword-message bug unpatched" "isic-3520 gas.sim broken on main" "the :approved-by architectural defect is still unfixed at the scaffold level" "19 of 20 consoles were never rendered in a browser; the two DADS markup defects found in isic-2431 may be present in the other DADS-styled ones" "14 linked worktrees left inside the shared orgs/cloud-itonami tree by earlier waves — reported, not deleted, since they may hold WIP" "docs/index.html still does not link the console in most repos (carried from Wave 4)" "no nightly regeneration gate (flagship item 4) — would be a murakumo fleet gate, not GitHub Actions" "phase-1 containment inversion in 31 repos (carried from Wave 4)" "cloud-itonami-isic-889 interrupt-before still not wired (carried from Wave 4)" "the tick's done-from-project-ledger still swallows parse errors silently; it should report skipped lines the way the edn-query loader's warn-skipped! does"], :note "20 agents dispatched, not 24: 4 of the tick's candidates already had REAL renderers on main and were recorded in the done-set instead of consuming slots. The stuck-pool defect was the wave's most valuable finding — it had been silently wasting roughly 20 agent slots per hourly tick, and the loop reported success the whole time because each wave's agents did real work on repos that did not need it.", :type :industry-stack/wave, :merged 20, :parallel 20, :success 20, :tick-defect {:symptom "pool stuck at 226 across 5+ consecutive ticks with an identical queue head; each wave re-derived work that was already on main", :cause "has-render? walked the local working tree, and west pins lag main, so landed renderers read as missing. Measured: isic-0124 has a 24KB render_html.clj on main (6deb159) while its checkout sat at d61a7e7 without it.", :fix "has-render? now takes the union of working tree and origin/main (neither view is trustworthy alone: the tree lags the pin, the local origin/main ref lags the last fetch); isic-dirs skips linked worktrees, detected structurally (.git is a file for a linked worktree, a directory for a real checkout)", :measured "pool 226 -> 221; isic-0124 no longer offered as a candidate", :cost-before-fix "roughly 20 agent slots per hourly tick spent re-deriving landed work"}}
