gents used mktemp -d).", :note "24 of 24 candidates landed REAL build-time renderers driving operation -> governor -> store, each with >=1 HARD hold enforced as a build-time invariant (-main throws on zero :governor-hold). Several repos have no langgraph wiring (isic-0126 1050 4321 561) and were driven through run-operation/run-proposal directly, expected rather than a blocker. Where a governor rule was structurally unreachable from the shipped mock advisor, agents injected a rogue advisor through the actor own documented :advisor seam rather than weakening the governor; governor, phase gate and store are as shipped in every case.", :harness-cap {:symptom "tick named 24 candidates; agent calls 21-24 were rejected outright with `Concurrent subagent limit reached`", :cause "the harness caps concurrent subagents at 20; the skill said --limit 24", :effect "4 named repos get no owner every round, and a wave recording :parallel 24 lies about its own fan-out", :fix "skill now says --limit 20 and states the cap; the 4 rejects were dispatched as slots freed, so all 24 still landed", :note "Wave 5 recorded 20-of-24 and attributed it entirely to already-real skips; part of that was probably this same cap unnoticed"}, :event/skipped-already-main 0, :event/pool-before 201, :event/type :industry-stack/wave, :worktree-path-constraint {:detail "child repos resolve langgraph/langchain via relative :local/root ../../kotoba-lang/..., so a /tmp worktree cannot resolve deps and the build fails; worktrees must be siblings inside orgs/cloud-itonami/", :status :recorded-in-skill}, :event/merged 24, :event/parallel 20, :mock-console-stub {:measured "9 of 287 cloud-itonami consoles in local checkouts are a wrong-domain robotics scaffold stub (robot-1 / deliver parcel), 2220 or 2063 bytes", :fixed-this-wave ["isic-3030 aerospace" "isic-5510 hospitality"], :remaining ["isic-6310" "isic-7810" "isic-8411" "isic-8569" "isic-8691" "isic-8810" "isic-9511"], :accounting-check "all 7 remaining lack render_html.clj AND are absent from the done-set, so the tick still offers them as candidates; the stub misleads a human reader but does NOT corrupt pipeline accounting", :separate-case "isic-4730 shipped a different fabricated console naming operators (Akita Fuel Mart, Atlantis Fuels) absent from its seed data"}, :approved-by-defect {:scope "fleet-wide scaffold defect, confirmed independently by 6 agents (isic-2592 2814 2393 4530 3250 + the isic-9522 reference)", :detail "operation :request-approval attaches the approver to the record :payload key, but store/commit-record! destructures :value and never reads :payload, so approval attribution never reaches the SSoT and survives only in the transient run audit", :handling "agents rendered it honestly (isic-2393 prints not-on-record; isic-3250 joins the approver back from :approval-granted audit facts) rather than printing a name the store does not hold", :status "still unfixed at the scaffold level; carried from Wave 5 not-done, now with measured blast radius"}, :event/success 24, :event/done-before 127, :abandoned-parallel-wave {:symptom "19 worktrees at orgs/cloud-itonami/.wave6-* created 09:10-09:17, ~80 min before this wave", :state "each held a written render_html.clj and modified deps.edn, ZERO commits, nothing pushed", :interpretation "an earlier Wave 6 did the work and lost all of it; invisible as a failure because nothing was ever recorded", :action "left untouched (another session uncommitted WIP); agents told not to copy from them", :follow-up "retire or salvage via git-cleanup-conflict; now redundant since all 24 repos landed real renderers"}}
