{:event/type :industry-stack/finding :event/wave 11 :event/at "2026-08-13" :event/kind :fabricated-console :event/note "Five committed consoles were hand-typed with content contradicting their own seed data, and one was hand-typed but seed-faithful. They invent PLAUSIBLE DOMAIN VOCABULARY, so a domain-name check passes them; only running the generator detects it. Fakes also tend to show ZERO governor holds -- whoever typed them was demonstrating success, so 'too clean' is a signal." :event/fabricated {"cloud-itonami-isic-6190" "CDR + SMS tables; actor has no CDR/SMS entity at all (CDR appears only as an evidence-checklist item name)" "cloud-itonami-isic-6619" "PAN validation + ISO 8583 MTI/bitmap/RRN; card.store docstring says it deliberately carries NO raw PAN field -- the fake advertised the exact surface the actor was designed not to have" "cloud-itonami-isic-6419" "accounts A1/A2 Acme/Beta Co, postings P1/P2, and ZERO governor holds; real seed is account-1..5" "cloud-itonami-isic-8411" "'Robotics Safety -- Operator Console' (mission M1, robot-1) in a public-administration repo; scaffold commit 4b01ca6 CLAIMS it was rendered from kotoba.robotics.ui, a namespace absent from the repo" "cloud-itonami-isic-8810" "same robotics stub, and the README documented it as legitimate shared-template output -- which is why it survived"} :event/hand-typed-but-faithful {"cloud-itonami-isic-4653" "7819 B, no generator, but every id/order-number/counterparty traces to seed -- 'no generator ran' and 'content is invented' are INDEPENDENT failures"}}
{:event/type :industry-stack/finding :event/wave 11 :event/at "2026-08-13" :event/kind :approver-attribution :event/note "Measured per repo, never assumed. SEVEN distinct behaviours across 20 repos -- a fleet-wide 'this repo has the defect' claim would have been false in at least 9. Wave 6's ledger called this a fleet-wide scaffold defect; that framing is wrong and should not be handed to agents." :event/behaviours {:fully-retained ["cloud-itonami-isic-7911" "cloud-itonami-isic-871"] :retained-on-record-absent-from-ledger ["cloud-itonami-isic-5629" "cloud-itonami-isic-8211"] :dropped-by-value-destructuring ["cloud-itonami-isic-1073" "cloud-itonami-isic-2821" "cloud-itonami-isic-8020" "cloud-itonami-isic-2399"] :split-per-effect-registry-rebuild ["cloud-itonami-isic-6520" "cloud-itonami-isic-4653" "cloud-itonami-isic-6619" "cloud-itonami-isic-6419" "cloud-itonami-isic-8411" "cloud-itonami-isic-8510" "cloud-itonami-isic-8810" "cloud-itonami-isic-6190" "cloud-itonami-isic-8610"] :no-store-write-path ["cloud-itonami-isic-0142"] :no-approval-seam-at-all ["cloud-itonami-isic-900"] :no-defect ["cloud-itonami-isic-8110"]} :event/dominant-cause "Not the :value/:payload destructuring bug. The common cause is actuation effects that RE-MINT their record from a registry sequence (registry/append, register-*, finalize-*) and therefore read neither :value nor :payload."}
{:event/type :industry-stack/finding :event/wave 11 :event/at "2026-08-13" :event/kind :governor-defect :event/repo "cloud-itonami-isic-871" :event/note "nursingcareops scope scanner does not read negation: run r08, a benign bed-linen supply request, HARD-holds because the advisor's own NEGATIVE disclaimer (投薬・医療用品なし) contains 薬. One of its six HARD holds is a substring collision, not caught clinical drift. NOT fixed in this wave -- rewriting a governor scope rule inside a rendering task is scope drift; needs its own change with its own tests." :event/status :open}
{:event/type :industry-stack/finding :event/wave 11 :event/at "2026-08-13" :event/kind :tooling :event/note "resource-guard.mjs refusal is NOT silently green -- both refusal paths call process.exit(2), measured under live contention. But a PIPE masks it: `resource-guard ... | tail` reports tail's 0 and discards the refusal. Separately, under parallel load it can die with EEXIST .../build/owner.json instead of the clean refusal, so a retry loop must match BOTH. One agent misdiagnosed this as a guard defect; the guard is fine, the caller's pipeline is not." :event/correction "Supersedes the in-wave claim that resource-guard exits 0 on lock refusal."}
{:event/type :industry-stack/finding :event/wave 11 :event/at "2026-08-13" :event/kind :verification-method :event/note "Techniques that discriminated, worth reusing: (1) isic-8211 diffed the stranded prior console against a fresh render and got EXACTLY ONE differing line -- its own bug fix -- proving authenticity and locating the defect in one measurement. (2) isic-6190 neutered the governor with with-redefs so zero holds fired, touching NO file, then confirmed -main threw and wrote nothing -- an invariant proof with no break/restore risk. (3) isic-8810 made the guard TWO-STAGE because a phase-gating hold carries empty :violations and would satisfy a naive hold count. (4) isic-8110 caught its OWN false positive: joining records to approvals on [op facility-id] is not unique, so an auto-committed record inherited an earlier approver and the page nearly reported a defect this repo does not have -- derive-at-render-time protects against staleness, NOT against a bad join." :event/caution "Three repos independently blurred 'governor refused' vs 'rollout gate held'; every page separating them into distinct tables is doing real work."}
