{:event/type :industry-stack/finding :event/wave 13 :event/at "2026-08-14" :event/kind :recovered-failure-modes
 :event/note "Six distinct ways prior-wave work was silently not-landed, all found by running the code rather than reading it. (1) NEVER COMPILED - isic-6493 unbalanced paren mid-edit (namespace would not read), isic-9312 unclosed form EOF at line 562, isic-0146 forward reference to a def ~190 lines later, isic-0149 (format java.util.Locale/ROOT ...) which clojure.core/format does not accept. Four renderers totalling ~3600 lines that had never produced a byte, two of them sitting on the remote LOOKING landed. (2) COMMITTED BUT NEVER PUSHED - isic-9810, one rm -rf from loss. (3) UNCOMMITTED WIP in worktree - isic-4662, isic-8720, isic-960, isic-0150, isic-0146. (4) HAND-WRITTEN FAKE committed - isic-9511 carried the known robotics stub (Robotics Safety, robot-1, deliver parcel, 2220 bytes) with no relation to ICT repair; isic-9700 historic console came from a root commit containing NO src/ at all, rendered from the dependency library unit-test placeholders while badging itself governor-gated. (5) SABOTAGE LEFT IN PLACE - isic-8220 worktree held an uncommitted edit that #_-disabled all six refusal scenarios (a prior agent proving the invariant fires, then stopping); the next build would have thrown. Archived to a patch before restoring. (6) SHIPPED DEFECT - isic-960 double-escaped HTML entities at 45 sites, so every scenario row read literally as intake &rarr; advise. Found only because verification ran AFTER the push, which is the ordering the skill mandates."}
{:event/type :industry-stack/finding :event/wave 13 :event/at "2026-08-14" :event/kind :not-done
 :event/note "(a) NO page was opened in a browser in any of the 20 repos. All verification is structural (tag balance by parser, CSS var closure, entity/placeholder scans). DADS visual rendering is unconfirmed fleet-wide for the 13th consecutive wave. Several agents cited the ~20-parallel-agent focus hazard and the runaway Chrome-for-Testing helpers on this host as the reason. (b) jp-go-dds treatment is now INCONSISTENT across the fleet and this wave widened it: isic-8220 pins 0a021805 not 83db9954; isic-8620 and isic-9810 deliberately did NOT add the dep, extracting DADS CSS from the copy the repo already vendors into docs/index.html so the build stays offline and matches the product face; isic-8522 lifted only the 22 primitives actually referenced (~1KB vs vendoring 67KB); others vendor the full stylesheet. No decision has been made about which is correct. (c) Stale agent/flagship-item2-* branches were left undeleted in all 20. (d) ~141 stray worktrees under orgs/cloud-itonami/ predate this wave (wave5-12 residue); agents removed only their own _wt13-*. Not removed blind - they may hold another session's only copy. (e) No fleet-ci gate was run against any of these branches. (f) DatomicStore path unexercised in isic-8620, isic-8720, isic-9511 - approver findings there are MemStore-only."
 :event/dads-hazards "isic-8522 measured that the PINNED jp-go-dds tokens/bridge-css bridges DIFFERENT token names than these consoles use - wiring it in naively silently unstyles the page. isic-2823 measured that --color-semantic-error-1 and -2 are BOTH dark (red-800/red-900), not a strong/weak pair, so using -2 as a tint background is unreadable; use the primitive -50 steps for tints. Both matter now that several repos rebased their consoles onto DADS tokens this wave."
 :event/repo-defects-left-open "isic-8522 academic-integrity check is unreachable on actuation ops - it reads a committed integrity screen, but the governor hard-holds the very screen that would write one; observed live, a flagged student certified anyway. isic-0145 phase gate erases a HARD verdict, cost escalations mislabelled :always-escalate, and commits never reach the store. isic-0146 same :always-escalate mislabel (high-stakes? merges cost-over-threshold with always-escalate ops). isic-960 Store protocol has no staff directory at all, so a staff-shift proposal can never commit and is reported as a missing CLIENT. isic-4662 store docstring claims approved-by-whom is always answerable from the immutable log; measured false - 10 approval-granted facts generated, 0 reached the ledger. All disclosed on the pages by render-time derivation rather than patched, since changing governor or commit semantics is a governance decision with its own contract tests."}
